<title>NETHERLANDS: AEA members NAtlantic load factor dips 0.5pts in '.</title>
<headline>AEA members NAtlantic load factor dips 0.5pts in '.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The overall load factor on the north Atlantic for the 26 members of the Association of European Airlines (AEA) fell by 0.5 percentage points to 72.6 percent in 1996, AEA statistics show.</p>
<p>This followed a drop in freight tonnes kilometres which had held back a rise in overall freight and passenger carried to below the overall rise in availabilty.</p>
<p>AEA statistics of flights to Canada and the U.S. with comparisons with 1995 include:</p>
<p>					  '96	 '95	  pct change</p>
<p>millions (m)						     96/95.</p>
<p>Freight tonne-km (millions)     8240.20   8370.05    down  1.6</p>
<p>Freight on pax services (pct)     72.6	72.9     down</p>
<p>0.3pts</p>
<p>Tonne-kms (millions)	     20490.9   19642.7     up    4.3</p>
<p>Available tonne-km (millions)  28207.4   26880.4     up    4.9</p>
<p>Overall load factor (pct)	   72.6	73.1     down 0.5pts</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
